{"name":"Butternut","hex":"#ffa177","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Butternut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Southern settlers of the Ohio river basin, who used dye from the  butternut tree to colour their home-made clothing","A Confederate Southerner, or somebody who supported southern rights and slavery .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Butternut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Juglans cinerea","blocks":[{"text":"Juglans cinerea, commonly known as butternut or white walnut, is a species of walnut native to the eastern United States and southeast Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Juglans_cinerea_002.JPG/330px-Juglans_cinerea_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juglans_cinerea","wikidata":"Q630288"},{"title":"Butternut squash","blocks":[{"text":"Butternut squash, known in Australia and New Zealand as butternut pumpkin or gramma, is a type of winter squash that grows on a vine. It has a sweet, nutty taste, when cooked, similar to that of a pumpkin. It has tan-yellow skin and orange fleshy pulp with a compartment of seeds in the blossom end. When ripening, the flesh turns increasingly deep orange due to its rich content of beta-carotene, a provitamin A compound."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Cucurbita_moschata_Butternut_2012_G2.jpg/330px-Cucurbita_moschata_Butternut_2012_G2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butternut_squash","wikidata":"Q4169287"},{"title":"Butternut (people)","blocks":[{"text":"Butternut was a term applied to inhabitants of the southern parts of Ohio, Illinois and Indiana in the early to mid-nineteenth century. Many of these settlers originated in the Southern United States, particularly Virginia, Kentucky and North Carolina. The term refers to the dye of the butternut tree, by which their clothes were colored. In the years leading up the American Civil War they generally supported pro-south and pro-slavery positions, often electing Doughface politicians. Their settlements hugged much of the border between free and slave states along the Ohio River."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Ohiorivermap.png/330px-Ohiorivermap.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butternut_(people)","wikidata":"Q104902324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Butternut_nut.jpg/500px-Butternut_nut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Butternut_nut.jpg/500px-Butternut_nut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A butternut","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButternut_nut.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg/1280px-Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-Juglans_cinerea_%28fossil_white_walnut%29_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossilized Juglans cinerea (fossil white walnut) in Pleistocene glacial sediments, Michigan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJuglans_cinerea_(fossil_white_walnut)_in_glacial_sediments%2C_Michigan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Dead_Butternuts.jpg/500px-Dead_Butternuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Dead_Butternuts.jpg/1280px-Dead_Butternuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Dead_Butternuts.jpg/500px-Dead_Butternuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butternuts killed by butternut canker","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADead_Butternuts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/500px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/1280px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/500px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stages of development of butternut squash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButternut_Developpment.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg/500px-Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg/1280px-Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":